 "steps": [
  {
   "caption": "This R has a full column, y = 1: every x is related to it. So ∃y∀x R(x, y) is T.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "grid",
     "set": {
      "highlight": [
       [
        0,
        1
       ],
       [
        1,
        1
       ],
       [
        2,
        1
       ]
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "ea",
     "set": {
      "text": "∃y∀x R(x, y) = T",
      "tone": "success"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "The same column puts a 1 in every row, so every x has a partner: ∀x∃y R(x, y) is T. That is the proof of ∃y∀x ⇒ ∀x∃y: reuse the one witness for every x.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "ae",
     "set": {
      "text": "∀x∃y R(x, y) = T",
      "tone": "success"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Now a cyclic relation: each row still has exactly one 1, so ∀x∃y R(x, y) stays T, with a different partner for each x.",
